{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122569","id":4309345598,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABANtlPg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122569","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122569.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122569.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122569","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122569/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122569/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122569/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/14eaf3018b38dca6a56cdd38c962e98580ec31c5","number":122569,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Windows: Fix Shift key handling by detaching it from raw input","user":{"login":"vorvek","id":9655848,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9655848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek","html_url":"https://github.com/vorvek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The current high polling mouse fix was done using raw input, and after that the shift keys ended up being processed from both the raw path and the standard path. Presses (and repeats) came from the standard queue while releases arrived through the raw input. The two queues aren't necessarily aligned as they don't share a common event order.\r\n\r\nWith this change, `_process_raw_input_event()` now only deals with the mouse, it no longer creates shift release events from `RAWKEYBOARD` data. Also, `WndProc()` no longer discards `WM_KEYUP` for the Shift key.\r\n\r\nAlso, each Shift key is tracked separately with the `legacy_shift_pressed` array. It wasn't exactly raised as an issue, but you could press both shift keys at the same time (maybe in a Pinball game?) and Windows could omit the message for releasing one of them.\r\n\r\nLastly, the recorded state is cleared after a focus loss, so that alt+tabbing or clicking out of the window doesn't leave the shift key pressed in the engine.\r\n\r\nI've tested with the original high polling test project to make sure it didn't regress, but I've updated my computer since and I get 600FPS+ at 8khz down from ~3000FPS when I'm not moving the mouse. I think that's probably okay and less noticeable in a non X3D CPU, but I'd need somebody else to test. @Calinou?\r\n\r\n- *Bugsquad edit: This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122554.*","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false